let $S = S(X,r)$ be its associated monoid,  and let $(G, r_G), (G, +, \cdot)$ be its associated symmetric group and left brace,
respectively.
We shall prove, see Proposition \ref{details_Prop1}, that
if the monoid $S= S(X,r)$ is embedded in $G=G(X,r)$ then $S$ is invariant under

