I’ve settled on a native Track B formulation that keeps the brace and Yang–Baxter objects visible. An instance is a finite radical-ring brace defined by a circulant bilinear form; the answer is not an index but a pair of monic affine polynomials describing the two coordinates of the brace’s canonical Yang–Baxter map at two displayed character vectors. The standard exact route is two full Horner evaluations, while the planted polynomial decomposition reduces them to a short low-degree calculation; generation carries those evaluations through an identity rather than solving the emitted instance.
